---
source: packages/tier2/regress/tests/iv.rs
expression: all
---
## the only instrument is constant
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ one
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 0 excluded instruments remain for 1 instrumented regressor
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, instruments: x ~ one)
  |           ^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula
  = help: `one` is collinear with the regressors and instruments before it and was dropped from the instruments

## the only instrument is a regressor
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ w
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 0 excluded instruments for 1 instrumented regressor
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, instruments: x ~ w)
  |           ^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula
  = help: `w` is already in the formula, so it is an included instrument and identifies nothing

## one instrument for two regressors
y ~ x + x2 with instruments: x + x2 ~ z1
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 1 excluded instrument for 2 instrumented regressors
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ x + x2, instruments: x + x2 ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula

## two instruments of which one is zero, for two regressors
y ~ x + x2 with instruments: x + x2 ~ z1 + zero
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 1 excluded instrument remains for 2 instrumented regressors
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ x + x2, instruments: x + x2 ~ z1 + zero)
  |           ^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula
  = help: `zero` is zero in every row used and was dropped from the instruments

## two regressors the instruments move only together
y ~ xa + xb with instruments: xa + xb ~ a + b
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: the instruments do not tell `xb` from the regressors before it
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ xa + xb, instruments: xa + xb ~ a + b)
  |           ^^^^^ instruments that move the regressors only together
  |
  = help: the first stage's fitted values are collinear: each instrumented regressor needs an instrument that moves it apart from the others

## an instrumented regressor missing from the formula
y ~ w with instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0504]: `x` is instrumented but is not a regressor
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ instrumented, missing from the formula
  |
  = help: add it to the regressors: `y ~ w + x`

## an instrument that is instrumented
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ x + z1
error[Z0505]: `x` is on both sides of `~` in `instruments:`
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, instruments: x ~ x + z1)
  |           ^^^^^ instrumented by itself
  |
  = help: an instrument is a variable outside the model that moves the instrumented regressor; a regressor cannot instrument itself

## a product instrumented as one term
y ~ w * x with instruments: w * x ~ z1 + z2
error[Z0401]: `w * x` cannot be instrumented as one term: a product stands for several
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w * x, instruments: w * x ~ z1 + z2)
  |           ^^^^^ a product on the left of `~`
  |
  = help: name each instrumented term: `instruments: a + a:b ~ z + z:b`

## one row
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0802]: no residual degrees of freedom: 1 row and 1 regressor
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ as many regressors as rows, or more
  |
  = help: a model needs more rows than regressors; drop terms or use more data

## an instrument that is not a variable
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ nowhere
error[Z0101]: no variable `nowhere` in `the frame`
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, instruments: x ~ nowhere)
  |           ^^^^^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: the variables of `the frame` are: y, x, w, z1, z2, one, x2, zero and 4 more

## instruments dropped, and the model still identified
y ~ w + x with instruments: x ~ zero + one + z1 + (z1 * 3) + z2
note: `zero` is zero in every row used and was dropped from the instruments
note: `one`, `(z1 * 3)` are collinear with the regressors and instruments before them and were dropped from the instruments
fitted: 3 estimates, omitted []

## a regressor collinear with the ones before it
y ~ w + (w * 2) + x with instruments: x ~ z1
fitted: 3 estimates, omitted ["(w * 2)"]
